+// Note [Path-weighted attention plan]
+// ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+// The attention plan (finish_sw_plan in model.hpp) gives every worker a share
+// of the work in proportion to its speed, and the slowest worker sets the
+// layer time, because the join waits for every section of a KV head. The
+// cost of a visit (one query against one page for one KV head) depends on the
+// path it takes: an AMX visit of a whole page is about three times cheaper
+// than an AVX visit, whether that AVX visit scores the whole page or a part
+// of it. Measured on delphi-3bda with the attention path stats, Muse Glimmer
+// (kv_mul 16), 2026-10-16: 1.65 to 1.7 us per AMX dense visit, 5.5 to 6.9 us
+// per AVX whole-page visit, 5 to 6.6 us per AVX partial-page visit. With one
+// unit per visit the planner handed the workers that held the partial pages
+// (and, with one cumulative sum, the pending pages) up to twice the mean
+// compute time per layer (tp4, prompt 1024: 3.30 ms against a 1.62 ms mean;
+// tp2, prompt 2048: 5.86 ms against 3.63 ms), while the AMX workers waited in
+// the join. estimate_work (model.hpp) classifies every visit
+// with the kernel's own dense predicate (is_dense_amx_page) and work() sums
+// the visits with the weights below.
+//
+// TRON_PLAN_WEIGHTED_DISABLE=1 restores the plan of before the weights: one
+// unit per visit and one cumulative sum over the ready and the pending pages
+// (plan_weighted_enabled). It exists for same-binary A/B tests and for
+// rollback.
+
+// Cost of one visit by path, in units of one AMX dense visit (the measured
+// ratio about 1 : 3 : 3, see Note [Path-weighted attention plan]).
+inline constexpr int64_t amx_dense_visit_cost = 1;
+inline constexpr int64_t avx_full_page_visit_cost = 3;
+inline constexpr int64_t avx_partial_page_visit_cost = 3;
+
+// The switch of Note [Path-weighted attention plan]. Read once per process;
+// exactly "1" disables, the same rule as TRON_AMX_DISABLE (amx_attn.cpp).
+TRON(inline)
+bool plan_weighted_enabled() noexcept {
+  static const bool enabled = [] {
+    const char* off = std::getenv("TRON_PLAN_WEIGHTED_DISABLE");
+    return off == nullptr || std::strcmp(off, "1") != 0;
+  }();
+  return enabled;
+}
